---
import { SitePage } from '@boombapbot/editor';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base
  title="Policies · boombapbot"
  description="What boombapbot keeps, the terms it is offered on, and what it is and is not."
>
  <SitePage client:load baseUrl={base} current="policies">
    <h1>Policies</h1>
    <p class="sb-lede">
      This page is short because the site does very little with you. I'll update it again before anything is for
      sale.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>You don't need an account.</strong> The machine works the same without one, and without one the
        site does not know who you are.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>If you make an account, I keep three things.</strong> Your email address. A scrambled form of your
        password that I can't read. And for each time you log in: when it was, the IP address it came from and
        which browser it was, so you stay logged in and I can tell you from someone guessing.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>I email you twice at most, and only when you ask.</strong> Once to confirm the address, and again
        if you ask to reset your password. Nothing else.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>One cookie.</strong> Logging in sets a cookie that keeps you logged in. Logging out removes it.
        There are no advertising or tracking cookies.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your work stays in your browser.</strong> Rhythms, tracks and knob positions are kept in this
        browser's storage on your device. They are not sent anywhere, account or not. Clearing the site's data
        in your browser removes them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Nothing is uploaded.</strong> Sound is made on your device, and exports are files your browser
        saves for you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No analytics, no ads, no third-party scripts.</strong> Three companies do the plumbing: Vercel
        hosts the site and keeps ordinary request logs, Neon runs the database the accounts live in, and Resend
        delivers the emails.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Deleting an account.</strong> There is no button for it yet. Write to me and I'll delete it by
        hand.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Terms</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>What you make is yours. Use your exports however you like.</li>
      <li>
        The site is offered as it is, with no warranty. It is a preview: things may change or break, and a saved
        beat may stop opening. Export the project file to keep a copy.
      </li>
      <li>Do not use the site to harm it or anyone else.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Disclosures</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        boombapbot is an independent project. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the makers of the machines
        it is modelled on.
      </li>
      <li>The sounds are synthesised here. They are not samples or recordings of any hardware.</li>
      <li>The faceplate and the machine icons are original artwork.</li>
      <li>
        Nothing is for sale yet. A one-time upgrade and a shop are planned. What they cost, how refunds work and
        what is collected to take payment will be set out here before either opens.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions come to me at <a href="https://mm.coffee" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">mm.coffee</a>.
    </p>
  </SitePage>
</Base>
